# Force PowerShell scripts to keep CRLF line endings on checkout: Windows
# PowerShell 5.1 fails to parse here-strings (@"..."@) in .ps1 files that have
# LF-only line endings.
#
# The BOM is NOT handled here, despite what this comment used to claim.
# `working-tree-encoding=UTF-8` is a no-op re-encode (git's internal encoding
# already IS UTF-8) and adds no BOM. It does not need to: install-windows.ps1
# is the only .ps1 with non-ASCII characters, and its BOM is stored in the
# blob itself. Every other .ps1 here is pure ASCII, which PowerShell 5.1 reads
# correctly with or without a BOM (verified with the 5.1 parser: 0 errors).
#
# Do NOT "fix" this to working-tree-encoding=UTF-8-BOM. Measured 2026-08-18 in
# a scratch repo: that mode requires the STORED blob to be BOM-free, so on a
# blob that already carries one git refuses outright --
# `error: failed to encode 'a.ps1' from UTF-8 to UTF-8-BOM` -- on checkout AND
# on git status, i.e. it breaks the file rather than improving it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Other shell scripts stay LF — they run on bash.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
